      "rationale": "This node is supposed to be about solving posed problems, yet much of the pool is bare arithmetic in disguise: Manny's item is the naked sentence 1 + 63, and the repeated 'Start at 60. Count up 20 more' prompts are number-line procedure, not a situation to be interpreted."
    },
    "comprehensive_coverage": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Picture-based problems do appear, but the story side is served by a single depersonalised frame -- 'One group has 33 items and another group has 51 items' -- with no named actors, no objects and no join-change structure, so the range of addition situations a Grade 1 pupil should meet is not covered."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Reading demand is low, each item is one step, and the counting-on phrasing gives a strategy the pupil can act out; nothing here exceeds Quarter 2 expectations."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Counting up from a start point dominates so heavily that it recurs in mcq, cloze and true/false dress; the few other shapes (number-line display, symbol groups, part-part-whole) each appear once."
    },
    "competency_alignment": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
